# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A.V. Jewelry Operations System — environment variable template
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. This file is committed and must NEVER contain a real value.
#
# Setup:  copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your DEVELOPMENT values.
#         `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed (ADR §11).
#
# Use SEPARATE credentials and SEPARATE Supabase projects for development,
# staging, and production (ADR §10). Never point local development at production.
# Hosted environments supply these through the deployment platform's environment
# variables, not through a file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Browser-safe (public) -------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are INLINED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE and are public.
# Only keys designed for public client use may go here.
#
# The anon/publishable key is safe to expose: it is protected by Row Level
# Security at the data layer, not by secrecy. Never put a privileged key here.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# --- Server-only (privileged) ----------------------------------------------
# ⚠️  The service-role key BYPASSES ROW LEVEL SECURITY ENTIRELY.
#
#   - NEVER prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would publish it to every visitor.
#   - NEVER commit it. Store it only in approved secret storage.
#   - It is OPTIONAL and intentionally left blank: ordinary application startup
#     must not require it, and nothing in Phase 0 uses it. Leave it empty unless a
#     specific, approved, privileged server-side operation needs it.
#
# Local Supabase prints a local-only service-role key on `supabase start`; that
# local value is not a production credential. Production values are never placed
# in a file in this repository.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
